# Alignment using Kallisto
		
## ******* ALIGN THE SAMPLE FILE ON INDEX FILE ********* ##
### Since the reading can either be single-end reads or paired-end reads the further steps will be done according to them being their single end or paired-end 
## for single-end reads; for doing this we will call the function quant and not ###index like before

kallisto quant\
-i kallisto_Homo_sapiens.GRCh38.cdna_index.index\
-o output_name\
-t 8\
--single -l 250 -s 30\
SRR######.fastq.qz

##### here we will take -l (length) as standard they are usually the length they take #while sequencing we do not know here, and -s (standard deviation), 
we will take ###default known values for both of it

## Use this code for the paired-end read file:
kallisto quant\
-i kallisto_Homo_sapiens.GRCh38.cdna_index.index\
-o output_folder\
-t 8\
SRR####_1.fasta.qz\
SRR####_2.fasta.qz\
&>output_folder.log      # this last line is not important to mention
